ull},{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-04-13T07:39:57Z","updated_at":"2025-04-15T05:22:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 24 Mar 2025 06:33:36 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7600 (RADV NAVI33) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen connecting a signal with the dialog, the generated method name will strip out any leading numbers from the node's name. Found it while having buttons named `20xButton` and `100xButton`. The editor setting `interface/editors/default_signal_callback_name` is set to its default value (`_on_{node_name}_{signal_name}`)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45651598-c05b-4c01-b023-88abb994b2ca)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a child node with a name that starts with a number;\n- Connect to any of its signals with the dialog.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[signal-dialog-number-stripping.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19724248/signal-dialog-number-stripping.zip)\nMRP's script has a method that was added by the dialog.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1"